| `models.allowed_hosts.<adapter>` | list of strings | `openai-compatible` gets `[]` | an adapter in `models.available` mapped to `host` or `host:port` entries, each in the one form `scripts/child_env.py` `canonical_host_entry` returns (a lower-case ASCII name, a dotted-quad IPv4 address or a bracketed compressed IPv6 address), none listed twice | `scripts/child_env.py` (`load_policy`, check_X); `models/openai_compatible.py` | Lists the hosts an adapter that sends its credential itself may send it to: `openai-compatible` refuses at construction a `base_url` whose host and port no entry matches exactly, and an entry with no port matches only the scheme's default port. A listed host is sent http only when it is a loopback address literal (127.0.0.0/8 or `[::1]`); any other needs https. An empty list, a missing key and an adapter not named all allow no host. Defence in depth, not a sandbox. | which variable is sent: `models.credential_env` | always |
